OCGRAPH 1
# Drone flight path -- a wide, continuous orbit over the landscape, with a gentle altitude bob so
# it doesn't look like it's riding a rail. Every node name states what it computes, so the file
# reads top to bottom like the formula it implements:
#
#   x = center_x + radius * cos(time * orbit_speed)
#   y = center_y + radius * sin(time * orbit_speed)
#   z = base_altitude + bob_amplitude * sin(time * bob_speed)
#
# orbit_speed and bob_speed are deliberately different (bob_speed is 6x orbit_speed) so the
# vertical bob never lines up with the horizontal orbit -- see BOB_SPEED below.
#
# Compiled and ticked by Aver.Graph's GraphHost (scripting/csharp/Aver.Graph/GraphHost.cs) as
# Tick(entityId, timeSeconds). GraphHost reads OUT pos_x / pos_y / pos_z, in that order, as
# (x, y, z) and writes them into the entity's CLocal.position (a Vec3 scene field) via
# aver_scene_set_vec -- NOT through a setfield node in this graph, because setfield only supports
# F32-kind fields today and CLocal.position is Vec3-kind (see GraphCompiler.FieldKindF32).
NAME DroneFlightPath
DESCRIPTION Circular orbit over the landscape with an out-of-phase altitude bob; ticked with (entity, time) by GraphHost.

PARAM time float

# ---- Tunable constants (all lengths in centimetres -- the engine's native unit) ----

NODE radius ConstFloat
PIN radius value out float 9000.0
# ORBIT RADIUS, cm. The sample level scatters content out to roughly 13000cm from the origin;
# 9000cm keeps the whole circle inside that scattered area with margin to spare, while still
# being a genuinely wide loop (the point of this drone is to cross a lot of ground continuously,
# for the chunk-streaming workflow driving off of it).

NODE center_x ConstFloat
PIN center_x value out float 0.0

NODE center_y ConstFloat
PIN center_y value out float 0.0
# Orbit is centred on the world origin.

NODE base_altitude ConstFloat
PIN base_altitude value out float 1400.0
# CRUISE ALTITUDE, cm (14 m) -- comfortably above landscape scatter height.

NODE bob_amplitude ConstFloat
PIN bob_amplitude value out float 180.0
# ALTITUDE BOB AMPLITUDE, cm (1.8 m) -- visible on approach, not a wild swing.

NODE orbit_speed ConstFloat
PIN orbit_speed value out float 0.15
# ORBIT ANGULAR SPEED, rad/s. One full lap every 2*pi/0.15 =~ 42 seconds.

NODE bob_speed ConstFloat
PIN bob_speed value out float 0.9
# BOB ANGULAR SPEED, rad/s -- exactly 6x orbit_speed. Six bob cycles per orbit lap means the
# vertical motion never repeats in the same place twice around the circle, which is what keeps
# this reading as "flying," not "riding a fixed rail."

# ---- Time input ----

NODE time Param param=time
# Reads the PARAM "time" argument GraphHost passes to the compiled delegate every tick.

# ---- Horizontal orbit ----
#   x = center_x + radius * cos(time * orbit_speed)
#   y = center_y + radius * sin(time * orbit_speed)

NODE orbit_angle Multiply
LINK time.value orbit_angle.a
LINK orbit_speed.value orbit_angle.b

NODE orbit_cos Cos
LINK orbit_angle.result orbit_cos.a

NODE orbit_sin Sin
LINK orbit_angle.result orbit_sin.a

NODE x_offset Multiply
LINK radius.value x_offset.a
LINK orbit_cos.result x_offset.b

NODE y_offset Multiply
LINK radius.value y_offset.a
LINK orbit_sin.result y_offset.b

NODE pos_x Add
LINK center_x.value pos_x.a
LINK x_offset.result pos_x.b

NODE pos_y Add
LINK center_y.value pos_y.a
LINK y_offset.result pos_y.b

# ---- Altitude bob ----
#   z = base_altitude + bob_amplitude * sin(time * bob_speed)

NODE bob_phase Multiply
LINK time.value bob_phase.a
LINK bob_speed.value bob_phase.b

NODE bob_sin Sin
LINK bob_phase.result bob_sin.a

NODE bob_offset Multiply
LINK bob_amplitude.value bob_offset.a
LINK bob_sin.result bob_offset.b

NODE pos_z Add
LINK base_altitude.value pos_z.a
LINK bob_offset.result pos_z.b

# ---- Outputs ----
# GraphHost reads these three, IN THIS ORDER, as (x, y, z). Reordering these lines reorders the
# axes GraphHost writes to -- see GraphCompiler's "OUTPUTS ARRAY" comment for why file order is
# the only order that exists once this compiles to IL. pos_x/pos_y/pos_z are Add nodes, whose
# default output pin is named "result" (see OcGraphParser.AddDefaultPins), not "value".

OUT pos_x result
OUT pos_y result
OUT pos_z result
